/target

# Beads / Dolt files (added by bd init)
.dolt/
*.db
.beads-credential-key

trees/
.env
*.sqlite
state.json
.mev-history/
# `/planning` (not `planning/`): a trailing slash matches directories only, but
# planning is now a symlink into the brain-owned vault (../_planning/mev). Anchor
# without a trailing slash so the symlink itself is ignored and never committed here.
/planning
node_modules/
target/

# Nested planning/ directories. The rule above is anchored (`/planning`), so it
# only ever covered the repo-root symlink into the brain vault — a REAL planning
# directory created anywhere below the root slipped straight past it and was
# tracked and pushed. That happened: engine-rs shipped
# crates/engine-core/planning/ (knowledge.md, memory.md, archived SDLC worklogs)
# to its public GitHub remote for weeks. Anchored-rule gap, not a one-off.
**/planning/

# ...except mev's own test fixtures, which are DELIBERATE nested planning/ dirs:
# the block-record checker's fixtures each need a planning/ tree to validate
# against. These are synthetic and must stay tracked.
!tests/fixtures/**/planning/
!tests/fixtures/**/planning/**
